/*
 * Retail state that no code in this port reads.
 *
 * Nearly four hundred and seventy symbols, and none of them dead. There are
 * three kinds here and it is worth telling them apart before deleting
 * anything.
 *
 * Most of it is the PSY-Q libraries' own state: the SPU and sequencer, the
 * CD-ROM driver, the GPU and MDEC command mirrors, the interrupt and DMA
 * tables, libc's digit and ctype tables. The port drives all of that through
 * its own backends, so nothing reads these, but they are the retail data
 * segment and they are carried whole.
 *
 * Then there is residue. Retail named addresses, not objects, so an array's
 * declared size runs on to the next named address and swallows whatever sat
 * between. Where the swallowing symbol is read and the swallowed one is not,
 * the swallowed name lands here while its bytes are still in use somewhere
 * else: the paths to all one hundred and thirty-five assets are read through
 * g_MsgNegconMaxTwist over in host_state_menu.c, and the names of the courses
 * through g_CaptionBestLapTime. So an unread name here does not mean unread
 * bytes, and the messages and format strings in this file are mostly that.
 *
 * Last, working memory. g_CdDirEntryName is five and a half kilobytes of
 * directory entries, g_CdFileCache and g_StEndFrame and g_CdRootDirLba
 * another kilobyte and a half each, all of them uninitialised: nothing is
 * being preserved there but the room.
 *
 * The sizes are worth reading with that division in mind. The biggest symbol
 * in the whole segment is here, g_MdecDpcr at sixty-eight kilobytes, and it
 * is named for a single DMA control register, so it is residue rather than a
 * buffer: it swallowed most of the MDEC region and carries more than half of
 * the initialised bytes the content lock folds. g_SinTable and
 * g_CellScanOffsets are initialised too, and those two are the ones that look
 * like they ought to be read and are not; the port computes both itself.
 *
 * Order is retail's address order, which is the only order any of this has.
 */

